{"school":{"dbn":"24Q019","name":"P.S. 019 Marino Jeantet","boro":"Queens","district":"24","district_label":"District 24","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"PK-5","status":"open","enrollment":1502,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"44-10 99 Street, Queens, NY 11368","phone":"718-424-5859","website":"WWW.PS19Q.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/70215","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"The Marino Jeantet school is a Community School in the heart of Corona. We pride ourselves on being a hub of the community at large offering robust services to both students and families.  We are a United Community School offering support to families in the form of food pantries, clothing closets, dental services and mental health services. Although we are the largest elementary school in NY, we create a family like culture though our monthly family events, parent workshops, and close Parent Association collaboration. We have afterschool programs Monday-Friday ranging from academic to extracurricular to ensure we are enriching the whole child. Our goal is to expose students to various, impactful experiences inside and outside of school to prepare students for their future.  Through our academic programs, school initiatives and strong community partnerships we aim to send students to middle school ready to begin college or career planning for a future of their choice. This school has a Bilingual Special Education (BSE) program: Open to students recommended for Bilingual Special Education (BSE) on their Individualized Education Plan (IEP). If your child is recommended for BSE on their IEP and you have questions, visit www.schools.nyc.gov/specializedprograms or contact BSEprograms@schools.nyc.gov.","start_time":"8:10 AM","end_time":"2:20 PM","languages":"Spanish","subway":"7 to Junction Blvd","bus":"Q23, Q48, Q58, Q72","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":null,"latitude":40.752701,"longitude":-